      "lastAssistantText": "Files reverted to clean HEAD. Here's the handoff:\n\n---\n\n## Handoff: Pure C89 AVIF Decoder\n\n### State\n- `stb_avif.h` is clean at HEAD (6859 lines). All session edits reverted.\n- C89 test builds with `cc -std=c89 -D STB_AVIF_USE_C89_DAV1D` but has ~14 `-Wlong-long` + ~5 other C99-extension warnings under `-pedantic`.\n\n### Goal: Pure C89 + correct output\n\n**C89 compliance fixes needed (apply to stb_avif.h):**\n1. `unsigned long long` (14 occurrences at lines 1958-2127) → use `stbv_u64` consistently; wrap typedef with `__extension__` for GCC/Clang  \n2. Enum trailing commas at `STB_PARTITION_V4` and `STB_LR_HAVE_BOTTOM`  \n3. `const unsigned short *scan` declared mid-block at lines ~2361, ~4671 → move to function top  \n4. `for` loop empty body at line ~5772 → put `;` on separate line  \n5. `0x0101...ULL` constants → cast to `stbv_u64` without `ULL` suffix\n\n**Decoder bugs found & fixes needed:**\n| Bug | Location | Fix |\n|-----|----------|-----|\n| Dequant `>>` dq_shift instead of `<<` | `stb_av1_reconstruct_block` l.4684 | `>>` → `<<` |\n| `tx_w`/`tx_h` = `blk_w`/`blk_h` mismatches coeff array | l.4846 | `tx_w=bw; tx_h=bh;` |\n| Skip context `sctx_y = above_nz+left_nz` gives 0/1/2, dav1d uses 0/2/3 | l.4851 | `(both)?3:(any)?2:0` |\n| `lo_ctx_offsets` indexed by pixel coords, not 4x4 sub-block | l.2422 | `(sx>>2)>4?4:(sx>>2)` |\n| `decode_symbol` returns `n_symbols` ~26% time → EOB overflow | l.2344 | Cap `eob_bin_val` to `3+eob_bin_sz` |\n| MSAC `r=0` / `rng_new=0` → div by zero | l.1971,2031 | Add zero guards |\n\n**Components to port:** CDEF filter, rectangular partitions, loop restoration (all ported earlier, reverted).\n\n**Test:** `./test_run_c89.sh` — currently ~7.4 dB average PSNR, target 30+. No images hang after EOB fix.\n\n[goal:blocked] stb_avif.h was reverted to HEAD. Re-apply the listed fixes to stb_avif.h, then verify with `cc -std=c89 -pedantic` and `./test_run_c89.sh`.",
